  "$schema": "../../schema/incident.schema.json",
  "protocol": "BIFKN314",
  "name": "BIFKN314 flashSwap lets addLiquidity mint against flash-depleted reserves",
  "summary": "BIFKN314 tokens are their own AVAX AMM: flashSwap(recipient, amountNativeOut, amountTokenOut, data) pays out, calls BIFKN314CALL and only then checks K, without taking the reentrancy lock that addLiquidity uses, and addLiquidity prices new LP shares off the current balance. Inside the callback a dust addLiquidity therefore mints LP against reserves the flash swap has just emptied, and after repaying the flash swap the attacker burns that LP for a large share of the restored reserves. The first attacker flash-swapped 405.07 AVAX from the aPHAR pair, added 0.405 AVAX of liquidity in the callback, repaid 406.69 AVAX and removed liquidity for 202.33 AVAX, then repeated it with 22.48 AVAX; eight attackers ran the same sequence against 24 BIFKN314 pairs on Avalanche through 2025-08-05.",
